.\" Man page for mermaid-export
.TH MERMAID-EXPORT 1 "2026-07-26" "1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mermaid-export \- export Mermaid diagrams to multiple formats
.SH SYNOPSIS

       mermaid-export [input.mmd] [options]

.SH DESCRIPTION
       mermaid-export is a Bash wrapper around the minlag/mermaid-cli Docker
       image. It generates publication-ready exports of Mermaid diagram files
       in PDF, PNG, SVG, and JPG formats.

       If no input file is provided, the script interactively lists all .mmd
       files in the current directory and prompts for selection.

       By default, all four formats are generated. Use exclusion or --only-*
       flags to control output.

       run (default)
           When called with an input file or via interactive selection, the
           script generates the requested output formats using Docker.

       list
           List all available .mmd files in the current directory without
           generating anything.

.SH OPTIONS
       -o, --output NAME
           Use a single base name for all output files. Extensions are
           appended automatically.

       --pdf NAME
           Set the PDF output filename (without extension).

       --png NAME
           Set the PNG output filename (without extension).

       --svg NAME
           Set the SVG output filename (without extension).

       --jpg NAME
           Set the JPG output filename (without extension).

       --no-pdf
           Exclude PDF from the output.

       --no-png
           Exclude PNG from the output.

       --no-svg
           Exclude SVG from the output.

       --no-jpg
           Exclude JPG from the output.

       --only-pdf
           Generate only the PDF file.

       --only-png
           Generate only the PNG file.

       --only-svg
           Generate only the SVG file.

       --only-jpg
           Generate only the JPG file. A temporary PNG is created internally
           and removed automatically.

       -w, --width WIDTH
           Set the PNG rasterisation width in pixels. Default is 6000.

       -h, --help
           Show a short usage summary and exit.

       --man
           Display this manual page and exit.

       --version
           Show version information and exit.

.SH OUTPUT NAMING
       When run without explicit output names, the script behaves as follows:

       o If an input file is given on the command line, the base name of that
         file is used for all outputs.

       o If no input file is given (interactive mode), the user is prompted
         to choose between:

         1) Using the input file base name.
         2) Using one common name for all outputs.
         3) Specifying a unique name per format.

.SH EXAMPLES
       mermaid-export
           List available .mmd files and run interactively.

       mermaid-export ERD.mmd
           Generate ERD.pdf, ERD.png, ERD.svg, and ERD.jpg.

       mermaid-export ERD.mmd -o Diagram
           Generate Diagram.pdf, Diagram.png, Diagram.svg, and Diagram.jpg.

       mermaid-export ERD.mmd --only-png
           Generate only ERD.png.

       mermaid-export ERD.mmd -o Report --no-jpg
           Generate Report.pdf, Report.png, and Report.svg.

       mermaid-export ERD.mmd --no-pdf --no-svg
           Generate only ERD.png and ERD.jpg.

       mermaid-export ERD.mmd --only-jpg -o Thumbnail
           Generate only Thumbnail.jpg.

.SH DEPENDENCIES
       docker (docker(1))
           Required to run the minlag/mermaid-cli container.

       convert (convert(1))
           Provided by ImageMagick. Required for JPG generation.

.SH FILES
       /usr/local/bin/mermaid-export
           The script itself (typical install location).

       /usr/local/share/man/man1/mermaid-export.1
           This man page.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
       PWD
           The script mounts the current working directory into the Docker
           container as /data. All paths are resolved relative to $PWD.

.SH DIAGNOSTICS
       mermaid-export returns zero on normal operation, decimal 1 on error.

.SH BUGS
       Report bugs to the script maintainer or open an issue on the project
       repository.

.SH AUTHOR
       Written by the mermaid-export user.

.SH SEE ALSO
       docker(1), convert(1), mmdc(1)
